Unity Advanced Scripting Guide
Comprehensive reference for advanced C# design patterns and scripting techniques in Unity. Based on GameDev Beginner’s design patterns series.
1. Inheritance
What is Inheritance?
Inheritance cho phép class con (child/derived class) kế thừa functionality từ class cha (parent/base class). Điều này giúp tái sử dụng code và tạo cấu trúc phân cấp cho objects.
Key Concepts

Base Class: Class cha chứa shared functionality
Derived Class: Class con kế thừa và có thể override/extend behavior
Abstract Classes: Class không thể instantiate, dùng làm template
Virtual Methods: Methods có thể override ở class con
Protected: Access modifier cho phép class con truy cập

Code Example
// Base class
public abstract class Human : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float health = 100f;
    public float moveSpeed = 5f;

    public virtual void TakeDamage(float damage)
    {
        health -= damage;
        if (health &lt;= 0) Die();
    }

    protected abstract void Die();
}

// Derived class
public class Player : Human
{
    protected override void Die()
    {
        Debug.Log(&quot;Player died - Game Over!&quot;);
        // Restart game logic
    }
}

public class Enemy : Human
{
    protected override void Die()
    {
        Debug.Log(&quot;Enemy died - Drop loot!&quot;);
        // Drop loot, give XP
        Destroy(gameObject);
    }
}
When to Use

Use when: Objects có shared core behavior dựa trên “what they are”
Good for: Player/Enemy systems, Weapon hierarchies, Vehicle types
Avoid when: Relationships không rõ ràng hoặc cần multiple inheritance

Pros &amp; Cons
Pros:

Tái sử dụng code hiệu quả
Dễ maintain shared behavior
Tạo cấu trúc rõ ràng

Cons:

Chỉ inherit từ 1 base class
Có thể tạo deep hierarchies phức tạp
Tight coupling giữa parent và child


2. Structs
What are Structs?
Structs là value types, khác với classes (reference types). Chúng được pass by value và store trên stack thay vì heap.
Key Concepts

Value Type: Copy toàn bộ data khi assign
Stack Allocation: Nhanh hơn heap, tự động cleanup
No Inheritance: Structs không thể inherit
No Null: Structs luôn có value

Code Example
// Struct for lightweight data
public struct Weapon
{
    public string weaponName;
    public int damage;
    public float fireRate;

    public Weapon(string name, int dmg, float rate)
    {
        weaponName = name;
        damage = dmg;
        fireRate = rate;
    }
}

// Usage
Weapon rifle = new Weapon(&quot;AK-47&quot;, 30, 0.1f);
Weapon copyRifle = rifle; // Creates a COPY

copyRifle.damage = 50; // rifle.damage still 30
When to Use

Use when: Small, simple data structures (&lt;16 bytes khuyến nghị)
Good for: Coordinates, Colors, Stats bundles, Config data
Avoid when: Large data, cần inheritance, cần null checks

Structs vs Classes





























StructsClassesValue typeReference typeStack allocationHeap allocationPassed by valuePassed by referenceNo inheritanceSupports inheritanceNo nullCan be null

3. Enums
What are Enums?
Enums tạo một set các named constants. Về bản chất chúng là integers nhưng có human-readable labels.
Key Concepts

Named Values: Dùng names thay vì magic numbers
Type Safety: Compiler checks valid values
Underlying Type: Default là int, có thể custom
Flags: Multiple choice enums với bitwise operations

Code Example
// Basic enum
public enum GameState
{
    MainMenu,    // 0
    Playing,     // 1
    Paused,      // 2
    GameOver     // 3
}

// Custom values
public enum Direction
{
    North = 0,
    East = 90,
    South = 180,
    West = 270
}

// Flags enum (multiple choice)
[System.Flags]
public enum DamageType
{
    None = 0,
    Physical = 1,
    Fire = 2,
    Ice = 4,
    Poison = 8,
    Lightning = 16
}

// Usage
public class GameController : MonoBehaviour
{
    public GameState currentState = GameState.MainMenu;

    void Update()
    {
        switch (currentState)
        {
            case GameState.Playing:
                // Game logic
                break;
            case GameState.Paused:
                // Pause logic
                break;
        }
    }
}

// Flags usage
DamageType damage = DamageType.Fire | DamageType.Poison;
if (damage.HasFlag(DamageType.Fire))
{
    Debug.Log(&quot;Burning!&quot;);
}
When to Use

Use when: Limited set of known options, dropdown selections
Good for: States, Difficulty levels, Directions, Categories
Avoid when: Values cần thay đổi thường xuyên, cần store additional data

Best Practices

Prefix enum names với “I” nếu là interface-like
Luôn set explicit values nếu order có thể thay đổi
Dùng [System.Flags] cho multiple choice
Zero value nên là default/none state


4. Async / Await
What is Async?
Async/Await cho phép execute code không đồng bộ, không block main thread. Khác với Coroutines, async chạy trên background thread.
Key Concepts

async keyword: Đánh dấu method là asynchronous
await keyword: Wait for task completion
Task: Đại diện cho async operation
Non-blocking: Main thread tiếp tục chạy

Code Example
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using System.Threading;

public class AsyncExample : MonoBehaviour
{
    CancellationTokenSource cancellationTokenSource;

    async void Start()
    {
        await LoadDataAsync();
        Debug.Log(&quot;Data loaded!&quot;);
    }

    async Task LoadDataAsync()
    {
        cancellationTokenSource = new CancellationTokenSource();

        Debug.Log(&quot;Loading started...&quot;);

        try
        {
            // Delay 3 seconds without blocking
            await Task.Delay(3000, cancellationTokenSource.Token);

            // Run heavy operation in background
            await Task.Run(() =&gt; ProcessHeavyData());
        }
        catch (System.OperationCanceledException)
        {
            Debug.Log(&quot;Task was cancelled&quot;);
            return;
        }
        finally
        {
            cancellationTokenSource?.Dispose();
            cancellationTokenSource = null;
        }
    }

    void ProcessHeavyData()
    {
        // Expensive computation
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; 1000000; i++)
        {
            // Work...
        }
    }

    void OnDestroy()
    {
        cancellationTokenSource?.Cancel();
    }
}
Async vs Coroutines





























Async/AwaitCoroutinesRuns on background threadRuns on main threadSurvives object destructionStops when object destroyedCan return valuesCannot return valuesNeeds cancellation tokensAuto-stops with objectBetter for heavy operationsBetter for frame-based timing
When to Use

Use when: Heavy computations, loading assets, network calls
Good for: File I/O, API calls, scene loading
Avoid when: Simple delays, WebGL builds, need tight Unity integration

Best Practices

Luôn use try/catch/finally với cancellation
Cancel tasks trong OnDestroy()
Không reference Unity objects trong background thread
Task.Delay dùng milliseconds, không phải seconds


5. State Machines
What are State Machines?
State Machine quản lý behavior dựa trên current state của object. Mỗi state xử lý logic riêng và transitions.
Key Concepts

State: Một behavior mode cụ thể
Transition: Điều kiện chuyển state
State Controller: Quản lý current state
Enter/Exit: Setup và cleanup khi đổi state

Code Example (Interface-based)
// State interface
public interface IState
{
    void OnEnter(StateController controller);
    void UpdateState(StateController controller);
    void OnExit(StateController controller);
}

// State controller
public class StateController : MonoBehaviour
{
    IState currentState;

    public IdleState idleState = new IdleState();
    public PatrolState patrolState = new PatrolState();
    public ChaseState chaseState = new ChaseState();

    void Start()
    {
        ChangeState(idleState);
    }

    void Update()
    {
        currentState?.UpdateState(this);
    }

    public void ChangeState(IState newState)
    {
        currentState?.OnExit(this);
        currentState = newState;
        currentState.OnEnter(this);
    }
}

// Example state
public class PatrolState : IState
{
    float patrolTime = 10f;

    public void OnEnter(StateController sc)
    {
        Debug.Log(&quot;Start patrolling&quot;);
        patrolTime = 10f;
    }

    public void UpdateState(StateController sc)
    {
        // Patrol logic
        patrolTime -= Time.deltaTime;

        // Check transition conditions
        if (PlayerDetected())
        {
            sc.ChangeState(sc.chaseState);
        }
        else if (patrolTime &lt;= 0)
        {
            sc.ChangeState(sc.idleState);
        }
    }

    public void OnExit(StateController sc)
    {
        Debug.Log(&quot;Stop patrolling&quot;);
    }

    bool PlayerDetected() =&gt; false; // Implementation
}
When to Use

Use when: Clear, distinct behavioral states
Good for: AI behaviors, Game states, Animation controllers
Avoid when: States overlap significantly, need parallel behaviors

State Machines vs Behavior Trees

State Machines: Fixed transitions, simpler logic
Behavior Trees: Dynamic priority-based decisions, more complex


6. Interfaces
What are Interfaces?
Interfaces định nghĩa contract - một set of methods mà class phải implement. Cho phép treat different classes như cùng type.
Key Concepts

Contract: Class phải implement tất cả interface methods
Multiple Interfaces: Class có thể implement nhiều interfaces
Polymorphism: Dùng interface type thay vì concrete type
No Implementation: Interface chỉ declare, không implement

Code Example
// Damageable interface
public interface IDamageable
{
    void TakeDamage(float damage);
}

// Interactable interface
public interface IInteractable
{
    void Interact(Player player);
}

// Player implements IDamageable
public class Player : MonoBehaviour, IDamageable
{
    float health = 100f;

    public void TakeDamage(float damage)
    {
        health -= damage;
        if (health &lt;= 0) Die();
    }

    void Die() { /* ... */ }
}

// Door implements IInteractable
public class Door : MonoBehaviour, IInteractable
{
    bool isOpen = false;

    public void Interact(Player player)
    {
        isOpen = !isOpen;
        Debug.Log(isOpen ? &quot;Door opened&quot; : &quot;Door closed&quot;);
    }
}

// Damage dealer
public class Weapon : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float damage = 25f;

    void OnTriggerEnter(Collider other)
    {
        // Try to damage any IDamageable
        if (other.TryGetComponent(out IDamageable target))
        {
            target.TakeDamage(damage);
        }
    }
}

// Interaction system
public class PlayerController : MonoBehaviour
{
    void Update()
    {
        if (Input.GetKeyDown(KeyCode.E))
        {
            Ray ray = Camera.main.ViewportPointToRay(new Vector3(0.5f, 0.5f));

            if (Physics.Raycast(ray, out RaycastHit hit, 2f))
            {
                if (hit.collider.TryGetComponent(out IInteractable interactable))
                {
                    interactable.Interact(this.GetComponent&lt;Player&gt;());
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
When to Use

Use when: Nhiều different classes cần shared functionality
Good for: Damage systems, Interaction systems, Collectables
Avoid when: Chỉ có 1-2 classes, hoặc cần shared implementation

Interfaces vs Inheritance

Interfaces: “Can do” relationship, multiple allowed
Inheritance: “Is a” relationship, single parent only


7. Scriptable Objects
What are Scriptable Objects?
ScriptableObjects là data containers tồn tại như assets trong project, không phải components trên GameObjects.
Key Concepts

Data Assets: Store data outside scenes
Shared References: Multiple objects reference same asset
Inspector Editing: Edit values in Inspector
No Transform: Không attach vào GameObjects

Code Example
// Scriptable Object definition
[CreateAssetMenu(fileName = &quot;New Item&quot;, menuName = &quot;Inventory/Item&quot;)]
public class Item : ScriptableObject
{
    public string itemName;
    public Sprite icon;
    public int value;
    public string description;
}

// Weapon stats as SO
[CreateAssetMenu(menuName = &quot;Weapons/Weapon Stats&quot;)]
public class WeaponStats : ScriptableObject
{
    public string weaponName;
    public int damage;
    public float fireRate;
    public AudioClip fireSound;
}

// Using the SO
public class WeaponController : MonoBehaviour
{
    public WeaponStats weaponStats;

    void Fire()
    {
        // Use data from SO
        DealDamage(weaponStats.damage);
        AudioSource.PlayClipAtPoint(weaponStats.fireSound, transform.position);
    }

    void DealDamage(int damage) { /* ... */ }
}

// Global variable pattern
[CreateAssetMenu(menuName = &quot;Variables/Float Variable&quot;)]
public class FloatVariable : ScriptableObject
{
    public float value;

    public void SetValue(float newValue)
    {
        value = newValue;
    }

    public void Add(float amount)
    {
        value += amount;
    }
}
When to Use

Use when: Data needs to be shared across scenes/objects
Good for: Item databases, Enemy stats, Global variables, Settings
Avoid when: Data cần unique per instance, frequent instantiation

Best Practices

Organize với subfolders: [CreateAssetMenu(menuName = &quot;Game/Items/Weapon&quot;)]
Use order value để sort menu items
Runtime changes không persist (unless saved explicitly)
Tốt cho data-driven design


8. Script Composition
What is Composition?
Composition xây dựng behavior từ small, reusable components thay vì large monolithic classes.
Key Concepts

Single Responsibility: Mỗi script làm một việc
Modular: Components có thể add/remove dễ dàng
Loose Coupling: Components không phụ thuộc lẫn nhau
Reusability: Dùng lại components cho nhiều objects

Code Example
// Health component
public class Health : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float maxHealth = 100f;
    float currentHealth;

    void Start()
    {
        currentHealth = maxHealth;
    }

    public void ChangeHealth(float amount)
    {
        currentHealth += amount;
        currentHealth = Mathf.Clamp(currentHealth, 0, maxHealth);
    }

    public bool IsDead() =&gt; currentHealth &lt;= 0;
}

// Damageable component
[RequireComponent(typeof(Health))]
public class Damageable : MonoBehaviour
{
    Health health;

    void Awake()
    {
        health = GetComponent&lt;Health&gt;();
    }

    public void TakeDamage(float damage)
    {
        health.ChangeHealth(-damage);

        if (health.IsDead())
        {
            // Trigger death
            GetComponent&lt;Destructible&gt;()?.OnDeath();
        }
    }
}

// Destructible component
[RequireComponent(typeof(Health))]
public class Destructible : MonoBehaviour
{
    public GameObject deathEffect;

    public void OnDeath()
    {
        if (deathEffect != null)
        {
            Instantiate(deathEffect, transform.position, Quaternion.identity);
        }

        Destroy(gameObject);
    }
}

// Movement component (reusable)
public class Movement : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float moveSpeed = 5f;

    public void Move(Vector3 direction)
    {
        transform.Translate(direction * moveSpeed * Time.deltaTime);
    }
}

// Input controller (player)
[RequireComponent(typeof(Movement))]
public class PlayerInput : MonoBehaviour
{
    Movement movement;

    void Awake()
    {
        movement = GetComponent&lt;Movement&gt;();
    }

    void Update()
    {
        float h = Input.GetAxis(&quot;Horizontal&quot;);
        float v = Input.GetAxis(&quot;Vertical&quot;);

        movement.Move(new Vector3(h, 0, v));
    }
}

// AI controller (enemy) - reuses Movement!
[RequireComponent(typeof(Movement))]
public class AIController : MonoBehaviour
{
    Movement movement;
    Transform target;

    void Awake()
    {
        movement = GetComponent&lt;Movement&gt;();
    }

    void Update()
    {
        if (target != null)
        {
            Vector3 direction = (target.position - transform.position).normalized;
            movement.Move(direction);
        }
    }
}
When to Use

Use when: Functionality không fit vào clear hierarchy
Good for: Mixed abilities, Modular systems, Plugin-style features
Combine with Inheritance: Core behavior inheritance + composition cho abilities

Composition vs Inheritance

Composition: “Has a” relationship, flexible mixing
Inheritance: “Is a” relationship, fixed hierarchy


9. Singletons
What are Singletons?
Singleton là globally accessible instance, chỉ tồn tại duy nhất một instance trong scene.
Key Concepts

Global Access: Truy cập từ anywhere qua static reference
Single Instance: Chỉ một instance tồn tại
Persistent: Có thể persist across scenes với DontDestroyOnLoad
Controversial: Dễ overuse, gây tight coupling

Code Example
// Basic singleton
public class GameManager : MonoBehaviour
{
    public static GameManager Instance { get; private set; }

    void Awake()
    {
        if (Instance != null &amp;&amp; Instance != this)
        {
            Destroy(this);
            return;
        }

        Instance = this;
        DontDestroyOnLoad(gameObject);
    }

    public void RestartGame()
    {
        // Restart logic
    }
}

// Usage from anywhere
GameManager.Instance.RestartGame();

// Generic singleton pattern
public class Singleton&lt;T&gt; : MonoBehaviour where T : MonoBehaviour
{
    private static T instance;

    public static T Instance
    {
        get
        {
            if (instance == null)
            {
                instance = FindObjectOfType&lt;T&gt;();

                if (instance == null)
                {
                    GameObject obj = new GameObject(typeof(T).Name);
                    instance = obj.AddComponent&lt;T&gt;();
                }
            }
            return instance;
        }
    }

    protected virtual void Awake()
    {
        if (instance == null)
        {
            instance = this as T;
            DontDestroyOnLoad(gameObject);
        }
        else if (instance != this)
        {
            Destroy(gameObject);
        }
    }
}

// Use generic singleton
public class AudioManager : Singleton&lt;AudioManager&gt;
{
    public void PlaySound(AudioClip clip)
    {
        // Play sound logic
    }
}

// Service Locator pattern (better than multiple singletons)
public class ServiceLocator : MonoBehaviour
{
    public static ServiceLocator Instance { get; private set; }

    public AudioManager AudioManager { get; private set; }
    public UIManager UIManager { get; private set; }
    public DataManager DataManager { get; private set; }

    void Awake()
    {
        if (Instance != null &amp;&amp; Instance != this)
        {
            Destroy(gameObject);
            return;
        }

        Instance = this;
        DontDestroyOnLoad(gameObject);

        // Get references to child managers
        AudioManager = GetComponentInChildren&lt;AudioManager&gt;();
        UIManager = GetComponentInChildren&lt;UIManager&gt;();
        DataManager = GetComponentInChildren&lt;DataManager&gt;();
    }
}

// Access via service locator
ServiceLocator.Instance.AudioManager.PlaySound(clip);
When to Use

Use when: Truly need global access, genuinely only one instance
Good for: Game managers, Audio managers, Save systems
Avoid for: Player objects, Anything có thể có multiple instances

Risks &amp; Drawbacks

Global State: Khó test và debug
Tight Coupling: Scripts phụ thuộc vào singleton
Hard to Refactor: Khó thay đổi sau khi đã dùng nhiều
Hidden Dependencies: Không rõ script dependencies

Best Practices

Chỉ dùng cho game systems, không phải game objects
Consider Events/ScriptableObjects thay vì Singletons
Use Service Locator nếu có nhiều managers
Document clearly khi dùng singletons


10. Events &amp; Delegates
What are Events &amp; Delegates?
Delegates là function containers. Events là special delegates tạo observer pattern - decouple trigger từ response.
Key Concepts

Delegate: Function pointer, có thể hold multiple functions
Event: Delegate với restrictions (chỉ class owner trigger được)
Subscribe/Unsubscribe: Add/remove functions với += và -=
Multicast: Một event trigger nhiều functions

Code Example
// Delegate definition
public delegate void OnHealthChanged(float newHealth);
public delegate void OnGameOver();

// Using delegates
public class PlayerHealth : MonoBehaviour
{
    public float health = 100f;

    // Event (better than delegate for public exposure)
    public static event OnGameOver onGameOver;

    public void TakeDamage(float damage)
    {
        health -= damage;

        if (health &lt;= 0)
        {
            onGameOver?.Invoke(); // Trigger event
        }
    }
}

// Subscribe to event
public class UIManager : MonoBehaviour
{
    void OnEnable()
    {
        PlayerHealth.onGameOver += HandleGameOver;
    }

    void OnDisable()
    {
        PlayerHealth.onGameOver -= HandleGameOver;
    }

    void HandleGameOver()
    {
        Debug.Log(&quot;Show Game Over screen&quot;);
    }
}

// Actions (generic delegates)
using System;

public class GameEvents : MonoBehaviour
{
    // Action with no parameters
    public static event Action OnGameStart;

    // Action with parameters
    public static event Action&lt;int&gt; OnScoreChanged;
    public static event Action&lt;float, Vector3&gt; OnDamageTaken;

    public void StartGame()
    {
        OnGameStart?.Invoke();
    }

    public void AddScore(int points)
    {
        OnScoreChanged?.Invoke(points);
    }
}

// UnityEvent (Inspector-assignable)
using UnityEngine.Events;

public class Door : MonoBehaviour
{
    public UnityEvent onDoorOpened;
    public UnityEvent onDoorClosed;

    bool isOpen = false;

    public void Toggle()
    {
        isOpen = !isOpen;

        if (isOpen)
            onDoorOpened?.Invoke();
        else
            onDoorClosed?.Invoke();
    }
}

// Advanced: Event with data
public class CombatSystem : MonoBehaviour
{
    public class DamageInfo
    {
        public GameObject attacker;
        public GameObject target;
        public float damage;
        public Vector3 hitPoint;
    }

    public static event Action&lt;DamageInfo&gt; OnDamageDealt;

    public void DealDamage(GameObject attacker, GameObject target, float damage, Vector3 hitPoint)
    {
        DamageInfo info = new DamageInfo
        {
            attacker = attacker,
            target = target,
            damage = damage,
            hitPoint = hitPoint
        };

        OnDamageDealt?.Invoke(info);
    }
}
Event Types Comparison








































TypeUse CaseInspectorProsConsDelegateFunction containersNoFlexibleCan be called externallyEventObserver patternNoSecureCode-onlyActionQuick eventsNoNo declarationSystem namespaceUnityEventDesigner-friendlyYesVisual setupPerformance overhead
When to Use

Use when: Decouple trigger from response, multiple listeners
Good for: Game events, UI callbacks, Achievement systems
Avoid when: Simple one-to-one calls, performance critical loops

Best Practices

Luôn unsubscribe trong OnDisable/OnDestroy
Dùng ?.Invoke() để null-check
Events cho public exposure, delegates cho parameters
Actions cho simple events
UnityEvents cho designer-friendly events


Summary &amp; Guidelines
Choosing the Right Pattern
For Object Relationships:

Inheritance: Core “is-a” relationships (Player is Human)
Composition: Mixed abilities “has-a” (Player has Health, has Movement)
Interfaces: Shared capabilities (IDamageable, IInteractable)

For Data Management:

Structs: Small value types (Vector3, Color)
Enums: Limited known options (States, Directions)
ScriptableObjects: Shared data assets (Items, Configs)

For Communication:

Events: Decoupled communication
Delegates: Function parameters, callbacks
Singletons: Global access (use sparingly!)

For State Management:

State Machines: Clear distinct states
Enums: Simple state tracking

For Async Operations:

Async/Await: Heavy operations, I/O
Coroutines: Frame-based timing

Best Practices

Start Simple: Không overengineer từ đầu
Refactor When Needed: Patterns xuất hiện naturally khi project grows
Mix Patterns: Không exclusive - combine theo needs
Document Decisions: Comment why you chose a pattern
Think Long-term: Consider maintainability và scalability


